Trimmed real data (ruling T1). http/pages.csv and http/services.csv are rows of
the CSV exports of two tabs of the HTTP Archive Web Almanac 2025 Fonts chapter's
results sheet ("Fonts 2025", sheet 1otdu4p_CCI70B4FVzw6k02frStsPMrQoFu7jUim_0Bg,
linked as "View data" from https://almanac.httparchive.org/en/2025/fonts),
downloaded 2026-09-26:

  gid 1668708562  Design: Which families are popular in CSS?
                  (30 of 200 data rows)
  gid 1594814478  Performance: Which families are used broken down by service?
                  (35 of 1,203 data rows)

Each file keeps the tab's preamble rows, its header row and the chosen data rows
byte for byte (CRLF line ends, the pivot-table cells to the right included);
the other rows are left out. snapshot/ is what almanac.fetch() makes of them.
The redirect URLs in http/index.json are invented: the real export redirects to
a signed URL, which is not kept.

The data is the result of the Almanac's queries on the HTTP Archive crawl of
July 2025 (github.com/HTTPArchive/almanac.httparchive.org, sql/2025/fonts/).
The chapter says: "© Web Almanac. Licensed under Apache 2.0." A copy of the
license, the repository's LICENSE file, is in LICENSE next to this file. The
repository has no NOTICE file.
